==Japanese==
{{kanji readings tab|左|ひだり|利|き|sort=ひだりきき|yomi=kun}}

===Etymology===
/hidarikiki/: [pidarikiki] → [ɸidarikiki] → [çidarikiki]. Compound of {{term|左|hidari|left}} and {{term|利き|kiki|effective}}. See {{term|左利き|hidarigiki}}. For alternative pronunciation: /hidarigiki/: [pidarigiki] → [ɸidarigiki] → [çidarigiki]. Compound of {{term|左|hidari|left}} and {{term|利き|kiki|effective}}. /kiki/ voices to [giki] due to [[w:Rendaku|compounding]].

===Noun===
{{ja-noun||hira=ひだりきき}} (''alternative reading hiragana'' [[ひだりぎき]], romaji '''[[hidarigiki]]''')

# the ability to use a left hand better than a right hand; [[left-handedness]]
# a person who can use their left hand better than their right hand; [[left-handed]] [[person]]
#* {{RQ:Nippo Jisho|229}}
#*: '''Fidariguiqi'''. ヒダリギキ (左利き) 左利きの人.

